  "summary": "Shaggy lion-barong versus widow-witch Rangda: Bali's cosmic combat enacted in mask, trance and gamelan.",
  "description": "In the Calonarang dance-drama, the Barong — a shaggy, gilt-crested lion mask on a jointed frame carried by two men inside a flowing mane — battles Rangda, the widow-witch with lolling tongue, pendulous breasts and claw nails. Followers of each rush in trance, krisses turning on their own chests only to be deflected by charm. Masks are sacred objects kept in temple pavilions, dressed in fresh offerings; the performance re-enacts rwa bhineda, the necessary balance of creation and destruction, in gold-leafed wood, horsehair and gamelan thunder.",
